geometries.prose_before:
The increase in same store sales resulted primarily from increases in our learning and baby categories. The increase in our learning category was mainly due to construction toys. The increase in our baby category was primarily due to baby gear and apparel. Partially offsetting these increases was a decline in our entertainment category primarily due to video game software and systems.
Gross Margin
The following are reflected in “Cost of sales”:
• the cost of merchandise acquired from vendors;
• freight in;
• provision for excess and obsolete inventory;
• shipping costs to consumers;
• provision for inventory shortages; and
• credits and allowances from our merchandise vendors.
We record the costs associated with operating our distribution networks as a part of SG&A, including those costs that primarily relate to transporting merchandise from distribution centers to stores. Therefore, our consolidated Gross margin may not be comparable to the gross margins of other retailers that include similar costs in their cost of sales.

geometries.prose_after:
Depreciation and amortization decreased by $34 million to $343 million in fiscal 2015, compared to $377 million in fiscal 2014. Foreign currency translation decreased Depreciation and amortization by $14 million. Excluding the impact of foreign currency translation, the decrease in Depreciation and amortization was primarily due to fully depreciated assets.
Other Income, Net
Other income, net includes the following:
• credit card program income;
• gift card breakage income;
• net gains on sales of properties;
• foreign exchange gains and losses;
• impairment of long-lived assets; and
• other operating income and expenses.

